WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.360
In DeFi, liquidity providers earn trading fees, but not all returns are guaranteed.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:23.040
When prices move, your deposited tokens may lose value, that's impermanent loss.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.000
Impermanent loss happens when the value of one token in a pair rises or falls relative

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.000
to the other.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.640
AMMs rebalance your assets automatically, sometimes against your favour.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:38.640
You added 1 ETH and 1,000 USDC when ETH was $1,000.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:45.680
ETH jumps to $1,500, but your LP position rebalances to less ETH and more USDC.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.280
You miss out on growth.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.880
High volatility, shallow liquidity and low trading volume amplify impermanent loss.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.920
The greater the price divergence, the higher the impact.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:03.160
Reduce risk by using stablecoin pairs, choosing high volume pools and leveraging tools like

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.720
concentrated liquidity.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.920
Incentives can help offset the loss too.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.320
Impermanent loss is a part of LP life.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.040
With the right strategy, your rewards can still outweigh the risk.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.880
Understanding it is the first step to long-term gains.
